    <briefdescription>
<para>Cumulative Student t-distribution. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Cumulative distribution function for <formula id="181">$ n $</formula> degrees of freedom (see mathworld.wolfram.com): <formula id="186">\[ F(x) = \int_{-\infty}^x\,f(y)\,dy = \frac{1}{2}\, +\,\frac{1}{2}\,sgn(x)\, \left[ I\left(1,\frac{n}{2},\frac{1}{2}\right) - I\left(\frac{n}{n+y^2}, \frac{n}{2},\frac{1}{2}\right)\right] \]</formula> where <formula id="187">$ I(z; a, b) $</formula> is the regularized incomplete beta function. </para>    </detaileddescription>
